# A patch file carries the line endings of the sources it patches as *content*:
# a diff of CRLF sources has a literal CR at the end of every context, + and -
# line, while its ---/+++/@@ headers do not. Line-ending normalisation cannot
# tell those apart, so it rewrites the file to be uniformly one or the other and
# the patch stops applying. Store and check these out byte for byte.
*.patch -text

# Same reasoning: these are exact bytes, not text to be normalised.
*.png binary
*.ppm binary
